%% Comparing slow-oscillation events based on peak ratio
% This script separates detected slow-oscillation events into two groups
% according to the amplitude ratio of the subsequent peak to the reference
% peak, using a threshold of 0.5.
%
% For each group, the mean thalamic signal is calculated within a +/-0.5 s
% window around the reference slow-oscillation peaks. The resulting average
% waveforms are visualized together with the corresponding slow-wave
% activity and event time windows.
%
% The mean amplitudes of the two groups are compared using an independent
% two-sample t-test. The temporal distance between the two largest peaks
% of each group is also calculated, and the proportion of events occurring
% within this peak-distance criterion is determined for both groups.
%
% The script further analyzes slow oscillations detected in the first
% thalamic channel by calculating the amplitude ratio and temporal delay
% between the reference peak and the subsequent peak. Events with a ratio
% greater than 1 are visualized individually to examine their waveform
% characteristics.
%
% Finally, raw slow-wave signals and neuronal spike trains are aligned to
% the reference slow-oscillation peaks. Mean waveforms and spike rasters
% are generated separately for the two ratio-based groups to compare
% neuronal activity around slow-oscillation events.

